Purpose: verify Phase 5 CSR file access, ECALL trap entry, trap handler CSR reads, MEPC update, and MRET return.
Memory model: instruction memory and data memory both use deterministic 1-cycle read latency. Data memory remains unused in this testcase.

Instruction flow:
1. addi x1, x0, 0x80 prepares the trap vector address.
2. csrrw x5, mtvec, x1 writes mtvec=0x80 and returns the reset mtvec value in x5.
3. ecall raises a machine-mode environment-call trap in EX.
4. trap control redirects fetch to mtvec=0x80 and records mepc=0x00000008 and mcause=11.
5. csrrs x6, mcause, x0 reads the trap cause.
6. csrrs x7, mepc, x0 reads the trapped ECALL PC.
7. addi x8, x7, 4 computes the resume PC after ECALL.
8. csrrw x0, mepc, x8 updates mepc to the resume PC.
9. mret redirects fetch to mepc=0x0000000c.
10. addi x9, x0, 9 and addi x10, x0, 10 confirm execution resumed after ECALL.
11. jal x0, done holds the main program after completion so it does not fall through into the handler.

Expected output:
x1=00000080 x5=00000080 x6=0000000b x7=00000008 x8=0000000c x9=00000009 x10=0000000a
